; Interprets: 3GPP TS 29.338
;; What TS 29.338's clauses state in prose about an AVP's value or presence,
;; read by hand and pinned to the sentences read (docs/constraints.md), in
;; clause order: clause 4's common aspects, S6c's procedures, commands and
;; AVPs (clause 5), SGd's and Gdd's (clause 6) and the result codes (clause
;; 7). S6c's commands are printed once under 16777312, SGd's once under
;; 16777313; ALR and ALA serve SGd too, under S6c's application (clause
;; 6.3.2.2), so clauses 5.2.2.1 and 6.2.3.1 both describe them. A rule
;; depending on a node, a feature, the subscription, the HSS's data or an
;; earlier message is `text-only`.


;; Clause 4.5, the use of sessions, in each command of S6c and SGd; the
;; two AVPs RFC 6733 defines are admitted through each body's * [ AVP ].
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: srr-auth-session-state
; AVP: Auth-Session-State
; Command: Send-Routing-Info-for-SM-Request
; Section: 4.5
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.3.0
"The client (server) shall include in its requests (responses) the Auth-Session-State AVP set to the value NO_STATE_MAINTAINED (1), as described in IETF RFC 6733 [20]."
    range 1


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: srr-no-authorization-lifetime
; AVP: Authorization-Lifetime
; Command: Send-Routing-Info-for-SM-Request
; Section: 4.5
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.3.0
"Neither the Authorization-Lifetime AVP nor the Session-Timeout AVP shall be present in requests or responses."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: srr-no-session-timeout
; AVP: Session-Timeout
; Command: Send-Routing-Info-for-SM-Request
; Section: 4.5
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.3.0
"Neither the Authorization-Lifetime AVP nor the Session-Timeout AVP shall be present in requests or responses."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sra-auth-session-state
; AVP: Auth-Session-State
; Command: Send-Routing-info-for-SM-Answer
; Section: 4.5
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.3.0
